    <h1>UX Research</h1>
    <p class="project-subtitle" style="text-align: center; color: var(--color-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">User research at the center of all my projects</p>

    <p class="project-intro">As a seasoned user experience researcher and strategist, I always start projects with asking: What is the root cause of the problem? What does our user really need? Specializing in deciphering complex human behaviors within massive, high-stakes data ecosystems, my research work bridges the gap between raw data and actionable product strategy.</p>

    <p class="project-intro">At enterprise scale, I have led cross-functional discovery and evaluation initiatives—most notably spearheading the foundational research for multi-million dollar Point of Sale (POS) and retail system modernization efforts.</p>

    <p class="project-intro">My methodology relies on rigorous triangulation: synthesizing large-scale quantitative data from millions of transactions and behavioral analytics alongside deep qualitative user insights to uncover high-value growth opportunities. Whether implementing entirely new software systems, mapping intricate operational ecosystems, or leading teams of researchers, I focus on transforming heavy cognitive friction into seamless, intuitive user experiences that drive measurable business value.</p>

